  "purpose": "U039 probe for the OPPOSITE failure of the pipelining fixes (controller note after rev-C017 F24): a flood of pipelined requests behind a request that stays PENDING must neither grow memory without bound nor leave sockets open. The service runs in a SEPARATE process with --max-old-space-size=48; each of three sockets holds one pending request (a submit held by the delay executor of the engine) and receives 64 KB blocks of `GET /x HTTP/1.1` up to 50 000 requests; requests and sockets are counted (no time bound): the child must stay alive, every socket must be closed by the server, the child holds no connection and a legitimate GET is answered. A CONTROL with the depth limit of the handler removed (the naive design) must fail. Expected exit 0 (real healthy, control not).",
